WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.017
Let us begin with the simplest Hugging Face workflow.

00:00:03.017 --> 00:00:05.372
First install the libraries.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:11.082
In a Jupyter or Colab cell, the exclamation mark lets you run pip from the notebook.

00:00:11.082 --> 00:00:17.492
In a VS Code terminal, type the same pip install command without the exclamation mark.

00:00:17.492 --> 00:00:21.507
Then import AutoTokenizer and load bert-base-uncased.

00:00:21.507 --> 00:00:26.302
The word Auto is useful because Hugging Face reads the checkpoint configuration and selects the appropriate

00:00:26.302 --> 00:00:29.562
tokenizer implementation.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:36.267
After loading the tokenizer, pass a short sentence to tokenizer.tokenize and print the pieces.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:41.152
Run the code exactly once, then replace the sentence with a technical phrase, a person’s name,

00:00:41.152 --> 00:00:43.757
or a rare word. Compare the resulting pieces.

00:00:43.757 --> 00:00:49.502
The point is not to memorize BERT’s token vocabulary.

00:00:49.502 --> 00:00:55.153
The point is to see that the checkpoint controls how raw text becomes the tokens the model understands.
